{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I will set My dwelling.</b> This is the Temple (Sifra; Eruvin 2)." "<b>And My soul will not abhor you.</b> — My spirit will not loathe you. Every גְּעִילָה is a term for the expulsion of something swallowed within something, as in ״כִּי שָׁם נִגְעַל מָגֵן גִּבּוֹרִים״ (II Samuel 1) — it did not receive the anointing, for they anoint a shield of leather with boiled fat in order to make it smooth so that the strike of an arrow or a spear will glance off it, so that it does not pierce the leather."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:37.788105714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}